speechtext:
-and see the position
they are in. The hon. member for Regina has been trying to impress upon the house that this is a marketing bill. But it is not a marketing bill, and this clause 12 and the amendment are just the opposite of a marketing bill. Under the previous clauses of this bill it is provided that schemes may be brought about. Under this clause and the amendment what is done?
The governor in council may, by order or regulation, notice whereof shall be published forthwith in the Canada Gazette,-
(a)	regulate or restrict the importation into Canada of any natural product which enters Canada in competition with a regulated product;
(b)	regulate or restrict the exportation from Canada of any natural product;
(c)	provide for the licensing of persons by whom any such natural product may be imported or exported;
Under previous clauses, power is given to the governor in council to approve schemes, while by this .clause 12 and the amendment you give the governor in council power to restrict imports of any natural products into Canada or exports from Canada. You simply knock on the head by this clause everything provided for in clause 3. Does my hon. friend from Regina, or does the Minister of Agriculture think that when the farmers become acquainted with this amendment by which the governor in council can restrict the export of any of their commodities by licensing-for if a man has no licence he will not be able to export, and the minister knows that-
